{
  "slug": "survey-question-writing",
  "concept": "Survey Question Writing",
  "generated": "2026-09-08",
  "summary": "A survey question is a measurement instrument. Bad wording does not just irritate respondents — it injects measurement error that downstream statistics cannot fix.",
  "facets": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "A survey question is a measurement instrument. Bad wording does not just irritate respondents - it injects measurement error that downstream statistics cannot fix.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#overview",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Default mental model: every question is a hypothesis about what the respondent will read. If two thoughtful readers could parse the stem differently, the question is broken.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#overview",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "1. Question-stem hygiene (Dillman)",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Stems must be direct, concrete, mutually exclusive, and answerable in one read:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#1-question-stem-hygiene-dillman",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "One concept per question - no \"and/or\" coordination across distinct constructs.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#1-question-stem-hygiene-dillman",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Common vocabulary - no jargon.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#1-question-stem-hygiene-dillman",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Concrete time window - \"in the last 30 days\" not \"recently\".",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#1-question-stem-hygiene-dillman",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Specified reference - \"your most recent purchase\" not \"purchases\".",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#1-question-stem-hygiene-dillman",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Symmetric framing - avoid \"do you agree that X is good\" (loaded).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#1-question-stem-hygiene-dillman",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "2. Likert scales: 5-point vs 7-point",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Default: 5-point for operational customer/employee surveys. 7-point when you need discrimination for regression/factor analysis.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#2-likert-scales-5-point-vs-7-point",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "3. Balanced anchors and label coverage",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "A balanced scale has the same number of positive and negative points around a neutral midpoint, with labels on every point.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#3-balanced-anchors-and-label-coverage",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Good: Strongly disagree / Disagree / Neither / Agree / Strongly agree",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#3-balanced-anchors-and-label-coverage",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Bad: Hate it / Dislike / Neutral / Like / Love (asymmetric intensity)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#3-balanced-anchors-and-label-coverage",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "4. NPS, CSAT, and CES — pick one per question",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Do not modify the NPS stem if you want to compare to industry benchmarks. NPS scoring: 0–6 = Detractors, 7–8 = Passives, 9–10 = Promoters.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#4-nps-csat-and-ces-pick-one-per-question",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "5. The agree-disagree anti-pattern (Saris & Gallhofer 2014)",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "\"Do you agree or disagree that [statement]?\" invites acquiescence bias (respondents lean toward \"agree\").",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#5-the-agree-disagree-anti-pattern-saris-gallhofer-2014",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Anti-pattern: \"Do you agree that the website is easy to use?\" (5-pt agree/disagree)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#5-the-agree-disagree-anti-pattern-saris-gallhofer-2014",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Better: \"How easy or difficult is the website to use?\" (Very difficult ... Very easy)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#5-the-agree-disagree-anti-pattern-saris-gallhofer-2014",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Item-specific scales reduce systematic error and increase reliability.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#5-the-agree-disagree-anti-pattern-saris-gallhofer-2014",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "6. Double-barreled and leading questions",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Double-barreled = one question, two concepts. Split it.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#6-double-barreled-and-leading-questions",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Bad: \"How satisfied are you with the price and quality of the product?\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#6-double-barreled-and-leading-questions",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Fix: Two questions, one for price, one for quality.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#6-double-barreled-and-leading-questions",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Leading = stem prejudges the answer.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#6-double-barreled-and-leading-questions",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Bad: \"How helpful was our amazing support team?\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#6-double-barreled-and-leading-questions",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "text": "Fix: \"How would you rate the support you received?\" (Very poor ... Very good)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#6-double-barreled-and-leading-questions",
          "note": null,
          "level": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "7. \"Don't Know\" vs \"Neutral\" vs forced-choice",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Neutral midpoint = respondent has an opinion but it is centered.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#7-dont-know-vs-neutral-vs-forced-choice",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "\"Don't Know\" / \"Not applicable\" = respondent lacks the information. Place it visually offset from the scale (Dillman) so satisficers don't select it by default.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#7-dont-know-vs-neutral-vs-forced-choice",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Forced-choice = use only when you genuinely need a side.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#7-dont-know-vs-neutral-vs-forced-choice",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "8. Ordering effects",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Question order: early questions can prime later ones. Put sensitive/demographic questions last. Put the headline metric (NPS/CSAT) before drill-downs.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#8-ordering-effects",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Response option order: randomize unordered option lists across respondents. Never randomize a Likert.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#8-ordering-effects",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Matrix straight-lining: long batteries of similar Likert items invite straight-lining.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#8-ordering-effects",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "9. Open- vs closed-ended",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Closed-ended = the default for quantitative analysis, benchmarking, large samples.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#9-open--vs-closed-ended",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Open-ended = use sparingly (1–2 per survey). Place after the closed question that primed the topic.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#9-open--vs-closed-ended",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "10. Mobile constraints",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Stem ≤ 20 words; aim for ≤ 12.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#10-mobile-constraints",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Scale ≤ 7 points (5 preferred).",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#10-mobile-constraints",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Avoid grids/matrices on mobile - collapse to single-question-per-screen.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#10-mobile-constraints",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Total survey ≤ 5 minutes for transactional touchpoints.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#10-mobile-constraints",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "NPS (canonical, do not modify the stem)",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "> How likely is it that you would recommend [Company/Product] to a friend or colleague? > 0 (Not at all likely) - 10 (Extremely likely)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#nps-canonical-do-not-modify-the-stem",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Generic attribute rating (item-specific, preferred over agree-disagree)",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "> How would you rate the [speed / clarity / accuracy] of the response you received? > Very poor - Poor - Fair - Good - Excellent",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#generic-attribute-rating-item-specific-preferred-over-agree-disagree",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Anti-Patterns",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Agree-disagree everything. Causes acquiescence bias.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Double-barreled stems.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Loaded adjectives in stems.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Endpoint-only labels on 7-pt scales.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Random Likert order. Never randomize ordered response options.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Modifying the NPS stem. Breaks benchmark comparability.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "text": "Stacking NPS + CSAT + CES + 10 drill-downs. Pick a primary metric per touchpoint.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/survey-question-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null,
          "level": 0
        }
      ]
    },
